.TH io_uring_register_spare 3 "October 22, 2026" "liburing-2.17" "liburing Manual"
.SH NAME
io_uring_register_spare, io_uring_unregister_spare \- attach or detach a SpareRing executor group
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <liburing.h>
.PP
.BI "int io_uring_register_spare(struct io_uring *" ring ","
.BI "                            struct io_uring_spare_reg *" reg ");"
.PP
.BI "int io_uring_unregister_spare(struct io_uring *" ring ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
SpareRing v4.4 is a research prototype and is not part of upstream Linux.
These functions require a kernel implementing the prototype.
.PP
.BR io_uring_register_spare (3)
attaches
.I ring
to a group of spare executors. Eligible runs of SQEs can be delegated to
these executors. The submitting task remains the SQ consumer and CQ
publisher, preserving the ring's
.B IORING_SETUP_DEFER_TASKRUN
completion discipline.
.PP
The argument pointed to by
.I reg
has the following layout:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
struct io_uring_spare_reg {
	__s32	attach_fd;
	__u32	nr_exec;
	__u32	n_max;
	__u32	u_pending;
	__u32	u_chunks;
	__u32	linger_us;
	__u32	mode;
	__u32	flags;
	__u64	cpumask;
	__u32	cpumask_len;
	__u32	resv[3];
};
.EE
.in
.TP
.I attach_fd
Set to -1 to create a new executor group. Otherwise, this must be a file
descriptor for an io_uring instance already attached to a group. The group
must belong to the caller's thread group; joining a group from another
thread group fails with
.BR -EPERM .
.TP
.I nr_exec
Number of executors to create for a new group, from 1 through 64.
This field is used only when creating a group.
.TP
.I n_max
Maximum number of SQEs in a delegated chunk. Zero selects the default of
32; the maximum is 64.
.TP
.I u_pending
Maximum number of unclaimed chunks for this ring. Zero selects the default
of 4.
.TP
.I u_chunks
Maximum number of outstanding chunks, including unclaimed and claimed
chunks, for this ring. Zero selects the default of 16.
.TP
.I linger_us
Time in microseconds that an executor polls for work before sleeping. Zero
selects the default of 50; the maximum is 1000.
.TP
.I mode
One of the modes described below.
.TP
.I flags
Must be zero.
.TP
.I cpumask
User address of a CPU bitmap for a new executor group, stored in a
64-bit integer. Zero allows any CPU. This field is used only when
creating a group.
.TP
.I cpumask_len
Size in bytes of the bitmap pointed to by
.IR cpumask .
.TP
.I resv
All three reserved words must be zero.
.SS Modes
.TP
.B IORING_SPARE_MODE_AUTO (0)
Adaptively delegate eligible runs according to the available executor
capacity and pending work.
.TP
.B IORING_SPARE_MODE_ALWAYS (1)
Delegate every eligible run, waking executors as needed, subject to the
chunk limits.
.TP
.B IORING_SPARE_MODE_NEVER (2)
Keep the ring attached to the group, but never delegate SQEs. The resource
freeze described below still applies.
.SS Registration rules
The ring must have all of
.BR IORING_SETUP_SINGLE_ISSUER ,
.BR IORING_SETUP_DEFER_TASKRUN ,
and
.BR IORING_SETUP_SUBMIT_ALL
set. It must not have any of
.BR IORING_SETUP_IOPOLL ,
.BR IORING_SETUP_SQPOLL ,
.BR IORING_SETUP_CQE32 ,
or
.BR IORING_SETUP_CQE_MIXED
set. No BPF filter may be installed on the ring. Registration must be
performed by the ring's submitting task, as required by
.BR IORING_SETUP_SINGLE_ISSUER .
A ring already attached to a group cannot be registered again;
this fails with
.BR -EBUSY .
Invalid settings, including nonzero
.I flags
or
.I resv
members, fail with
.BR -EINVAL .
.PP
The underlying
.B IORING_REGISTER_SPARE
operation takes this structure as its argument and requires
.I nr_args
to be 1. The liburing helper supplies this value.
.SS Eligible operations
Only
.BR IORING_OP_READ ,
.BR IORING_OP_WRITE ,
.BR IORING_OP_READ_FIXED ,
and
.B IORING_OP_WRITE_FIXED
are eligible for delegation. An SQE may have
.B IOSQE_FIXED_FILE
set, but no other SQE flags, and must have zero
.I personality
and
.IR attr_type_mask .
Linked or drained SQEs, vectored I/O, and operations with indirect input
descriptors are handled by the normal submission path. Eligibility does
not change the application's obligation to keep I/O buffers valid until
completion.
.SS Resource freeze
While attached, fixed file and buffer tables cannot change
.RB ( -EBUSY ).
Register fixed files and buffers before attaching the ring, even in
.BR IORING_SPARE_MODE_NEVER .
The freeze covers registering, unregistering, updating, and cloning into
these tables, changing the fixed file allocation range, and registering a
BPF filter. It also covers operations that install or remove direct file
descriptors, including incoming
.B IORING_MSG_SEND_FD
messages, and kernel buffer registration and unregistration.
.PP
.BR io_uring_unregister_spare (3)
detaches the ring from its group. The resource freeze persists after
detachment while any delegated chunk remains outstanding. Drive and drain
outstanding completions before changing the tables; such changes can
continue to return
.B -EBUSY
until the chunks have been retired.
.PP
The underlying
.B IORING_UNREGISTER_SPARE
operation requires a NULL argument and
.I nr_args
of 0. The liburing helper supplies these values.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, these functions return 0. On failure, they return a negative
error code.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B -EINVAL
The kernel does not implement SpareRing, the ring is incompatible, or the
registration arguments are invalid.
.TP
.B -EOPNOTSUPP
The kernel does not support the requested SpareRing operation.
.TP
.B -EBUSY
The ring is already attached to a group.
.TP
.B -EPERM
The executor group named by
.I attach_fd
belongs to a different thread group.
.TP
.B -ENOMEM
Insufficient memory to create the executor group or attachment.
.TP
.B -EFAULT
An argument or CPU bitmap address is invalid.
.SH EXAMPLES
.in +4n
.EX
struct io_uring ring;
struct io_uring_spare_reg reg = {
	.attach_fd = -1,
	.nr_exec = 2,
	.mode = IORING_SPARE_MODE_ALWAYS,
};
unsigned int flags = IORING_SETUP_SINGLE_ISSUER |
		     IORING_SETUP_DEFER_TASKRUN |
		     IORING_SETUP_SUBMIT_ALL;
int ret;

ret = io_uring_queue_init(256, &ring, flags);
if (ret)
	return ret;
/* Register any fixed files and buffers here, before attaching. */
ret = io_uring_register_spare(&ring, &reg);
if (ret) {
	io_uring_queue_exit(&ring);
	return ret;
}
/* Submit I/O and consume completions here. */
ret = io_uring_unregister_spare(&ring);
/* Drain outstanding I/O before changing fixed resource tables. */
io_uring_queue_exit(&ring);
return ret;
.EE
.in
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR io_uring_setup (2),
.BR io_uring_register (2),
.BR io_uring_register_files (3),
.BR io_uring_register_buffers (3),
.BR io_uring_submit (3)
